+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope, Cancelling Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 put "changing or cancelling a visit once booked" out of scope. The row was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08. [That ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) set the rule for reopening it: only an explicit owner decision recorded at intake reopens the row, never a request by implication.
+
+On 2026-08-17 the owner made that decision. The request reported that visits can be created but never corrected, and narrowed the row in the same breath. The row bundled two capabilities under one line, so the decision had to say which half moved.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner decided otherwise, and the row's own convention makes an owner decision the way it changes.
+2. **Retire NG-5 entirely.** Rejected: it would open cancellation too. The owner kept cancellation out, and the lifecycle-state reason that justified the row still covers it.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen). Correction joins the forward-only correction the sample already demonstrates for owner and pet details; cancellation keeps the row.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's decision, verbatim: "Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in."
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is a requirement, `REQ-VISITEDIT-001`. Cancelling a booked visit remains NG-5. The correction applies to the visit already recorded — it is not a second booking, so a corrected visit leaves the pet's visit count unchanged.
+
+The owner also decided the capability ships without a visible entry point: "The edit form is reachable by its URL alone: the owner detail page gains no edit link in this request. A visible entry point may come as a follow-up request."
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample no longer treats a booked visit as immutable. It still deletes nothing: NG-4 stands whole, and a booked visit cannot be cancelled.
+- The correction form is discoverable only to a reader who knows its address. Adding a link is a follow-up request, recorded as an open question.
+- Two questions the request did not settle stay open in the PRD. Whether a past visit can be corrected under the booking date rule is one; which page would carry an entry point is the other.
+- Reopening the remaining half of NG-5 needs a recorded owner decision, exactly as this narrowing did.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [REQ-VISITEDIT-001](../prd.md#req-visitedit-001) — the capability the narrowing admits.
