@@ -114,6 +114,28 @@ A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
 
+### Correcting a booked visit
+
+<a id="req-visitedit-001"></a>
+
+A booked visit's date and description can be corrected after the fact. The correction lands on that same visit; the pet gains no second visit from it `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. The correction form opens on the visit's current date and description, and a correction is checked exactly as a booking is. An accepted correction returns the reader to the owner's record. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope (NG-5).
+
+The capability has no visible entry point in this requirement: the correction form is reached by its own address, and no page offers a link to it. Adding one is a separate request.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when its correction form is opened, then the form shows that visit's current date and description.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when a description and a date later than today are submitted, then that visit carries the new values and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when a correction is accepted, then the pet holds the same number of visits as before.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused and the description is named.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused and the date is named.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a refused correction, when the form is shown again, then it carries the submitted values and the reason for the refusal.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A correction naming a visit that does not belong to the named pet is refused rather than applied. The same holds for a pet that does not belong to the named owner.
+2. A correction leaves the visit on the same pet; a visit cannot be moved to another pet.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope, Cancelling Is Not](adr/2026-08-17-non-goal-visit-correction.md)
+
